e’s a quick demo:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/55bc2a39-fa75-478b-b1c1-d0ff81003023","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2969879635/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970769729","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103272#issuecomment-2970769729","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103272","id":2970769729,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xEllB","user":{"login":"SanNull","id":124409014,"node_id":"U_kgDOB2pUtg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124409014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull","html_url":"https://github.com/SanNull","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SanNull/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T15:35:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T15:36:38Z","body":"> [...] The reason is that the most of users will always only select one of the options\n\nSince most users will prefer one over the other, wouldn't it be better if the option was only located in the Editor Settings? I'm suggesting this because Timeline's buttons don't retain state after the editor is closed, so the user would have to set the option in the Editor Settings either way. It'd be interesting to discuss about GUI elements remembering their state, but for now, I think adding this only in the Settings should suffice.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970769729/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]